.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt PWD 1
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm pwd
.Nd write the working directory's name
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl L | P
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
writes the absolute pathname of the working directory.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl L
The logical name, the default: the value of
.Ev PWD ,
if it is an absolute pathname of the working directory with no
.Pa \&.
or
.Pa ..
component; otherwise as for
.Fl P .
.It Fl P
The physical name, with no symbolic links.
.El
.Pp
The last of the two counts.
Shells have a
.Ic pwd
built-in that keeps
.Ev PWD
itself.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "PWD"
.It Ev PWD
The logical working directory, as set by the shell's
.Ic cd .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cd 1 ,
.Xr realpath 1 ,
.Xr sh 1 ,
.Xr getcwd 3
.Sh STANDARDS
.Nm
conforms to
.St -p1003.1-2008 .
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
command appeared in
.At v5 .
